// Figure 4.2 — Sequence diagram: ingesting and scoring a transaction
// Eraser: New diagram > Sequence diagram, paste this code.
title Ingest and score a transaction

Simulator [icon: send, color: gray]
Ingest API [icon: server, color: blue]
Store [icon: layers, color: blue]
Inference service [icon: cpu, color: purple]
PostgreSQL [icon: database, color: green]
Dashboard (browser) [icon: monitor, color: orange]

Simulator > Ingest API: POST /api/transactions (X-Api-Key, 30 features, optional label)
activate Ingest API
Ingest API > Ingest API: verify API key (constant-time SHA-256 compare)
alt [label: invalid key, color: red] {
  Ingest API --> Simulator: 401 Invalid API key
}
Ingest API > Ingest API: validate against the contract (zod)
alt [label: invalid record, color: red] {
  Ingest API --> Simulator: 400 with the failing fields
}
Ingest API > Store: existing transaction id?
Store > PostgreSQL: SELECT id FROM transactions
alt [label: duplicate, color: orange] {
  Ingest API --> Simulator: 409 Duplicate transaction ID
}
Ingest API > Store: current threshold (5 s cache)
Ingest API > Inference service: POST /predict (features only, 800 ms timeout)
activate Inference service
Inference service > Inference service: scale Time and Amount, run CNN
Inference service --> Ingest API: probability, model version (+ shadow score)
deactivate Inference service
Ingest API > Ingest API: isHighRisk(probability, threshold)
Ingest API > Store: commit transaction (+ alert if high risk) + daily stats
activate Store
Store > PostgreSQL: BEGIN; INSERT transaction; INSERT alert; UPSERT daily_stats; COMMIT
Store --> Dashboard (browser): SSE events: transaction, alert, stats
deactivate Store
Ingest API --> Simulator: 201 probability, risk level, threshold used, latency
deactivate Ingest API
